,"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLPartList.Item"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPartList":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartlist","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartList","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPartList","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The part-list identifies the different musical parts in this document. Each part has an ID that is used later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within the musical data. Since parts may be encoded separately and combined later, identification elements are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"present at both the score and score-part levels. There must be at least one score-part, combined as desired","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with part-group elements that indicate braces and brackets. Parts are ordered from top to bottom in a score","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"based on the order in which they appear in the part-list.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPartList","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLPartList"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPartList/Item/scorePart(_:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartlist\/item\/scorepart(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartList\/Item\/scorePart(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scorePart","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLScorePart","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLScorePartV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The score-part element is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the part-list element.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"MXLPartList.Item.scorePart(_:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLScorePart":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlscorepart","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLScorePart","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLScorePart","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The score-part type collects part-wide information for each part in a score. Often, each MusicXML part","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corresponds to a track in a Standard MIDI Format 1 file. In this case, the midi-device element is used to make","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a MIDI device or port assignment for the given track or specific MIDI instruments. Initial midi-instrument","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assignments may be made here as well. The score-instrument elements are used when there are multiple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instruments per track.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLScorePart","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLScorePart"}}}